%description:

Tcp.notsentLowat:mark -- when the unsent bytes fall to the mark, the application gets one send-ready indication.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "when they exceed it, TCP sends no TCP_I_SEND_MSG until they are at or
below it again, and then it sends one".

The classes: off (-1B, the default), mark (0B and more), and socket-override: a
TCP_NOTSENT_LOWAT of the socket takes the place of the parameter. The code: the indication
TCP_I_SEND_MSG when the unsent bytes fall to the mark (TcpConnection::sendData()), and the
socket option in initConnection(). This test separates "mark" from "off".

Host under test: host1, with 4096 bytes, whose application writes 100000 bytes after the
handshake. Observation: level 1 at the application: one socketSendReady.

%# parameter: Tcp.notsentLowat
%# class: mark
%# value: 4096B
%# key: *.host1.tcp.notsentLowat
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpNotsentLowatMark")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.app[0]").signal("socketEstablished").within(0.1))
        .act(action().after(0.001).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.sendData(app.socket(), 100000);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.app[0]").signal("socketSendReady")
              .describe("the send-ready indication")
              .within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpNotsentLowatMark compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.notsentLowat = 4096B    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpNotsentLowatMark: PASS
